:: mall.taylor.first-meeting -> @exit
  @place-key mall
  @auto enter-place
  @priority 500
  @when npc.taylor.present and not npc.taylor.met
  @onenter
    @effect relationship taylor.friendship 1
  @endonenter

  As you pass the entrance to the food court, someone a few steps away slows down and looks at you twice.

  "Hey- you're at my school, aren't you?" {{npc.taylor.subject}} asks. "I'm Taylor. I've seen you around, but I don't think we've actually met."

  You introduce yourself, and Taylor smiles as if {{npc.taylor.subject}} has solved a small mystery. You talk for a few minutes about school and the shops before the crowd begins to carry you in different directions.

  @next "See you at school" -> @exit

:: place.mall
  @hub mall
  @choices "Things to do"

  Music and conversation echo through the bright galleries of {{place.name}}. Shop windows compete for attention around the central atrium.

  @choice "Browse the shops" -> mall.browse
    @icon 🛍️
    @time 45m
  @endchoice

  @choice "Visit the food court" -> mall.food-court
    @icon 🍜
  @endchoice

  @choice "Visit the electronics shop" -> mall.electronics
    @icon 💻
  @endchoice

:: mall.browse -> @exit
  You wander between crowded clothes shops, cosmetics counters, bookshops and kiosks. Nothing demands to be bought today, but the window displays make sure you consider it.

:: mall.food-court
  @heading "The food court"

  The tables overlook a ring of glowing menu boards. The air smells of coffee, hot oil and too many different lunches at once.

  @choice "Buy a meal" -> @exit
    @time 30m
    @when player.money >= 8
    @change money -8 "£8 meal"
    @change stat stress -5
    @response
      You find a free table and eat while watching shoppers cross the atrium below.
    @endresponse
  @endchoice

  @choice "I can't afford a meal" -> @exit
    @when player.money < 8
    @response
      You study the menu boards, then decide that looking is free.
    @endresponse
  @endchoice

  @choice "Return to the atrium" -> @exit
  @endchoice

:: mall.electronics
  @heading "Electronics"

  Laptops, monitors and carefully lit desktop computers cover the display tables. A boxed home computer costs £600 and includes everything needed to get online.

  @choice "Buy a home computer" -> @exit
    @time 15m
    @when player.money >= 600 and not flags.inventory.computer
    @change money -600 "£600 computer"
    @effect set flags.inventory.computer
    @response
      A clerk rings up the computer and arranges delivery to your home. [info]You now own a home computer.[/info]
    @endresponse
  @endchoice

  @choice "The computer is too expensive" -> @exit
    @when player.money < 600 and not flags.inventory.computer
    @response
      You check the price twice. It is going to take more saving before you can bring one home.
    @endresponse
  @endchoice

  @choice "Look at accessories" -> @exit
    @when flags.inventory.computer
    @response
      You already have the important part. The walls of accessories can wait until you actually need something.
    @endresponse
  @endchoice

  @choice "Return to the atrium" -> @exit
  @endchoice
